# Bare SELECT DATABASE() / SCHEMA() report the connection's current database.
#
# A bare `SELECT DATABASE()` (and the other connection-probe SELECTs) is answered
# by the server's session fast-path before the parser sees it. That fast-path
# returned a hard-coded NULL for DATABASE() / SCHEMA(), so a connection that had
# selected a database still saw NULL -- even though the parser already folded
# DATABASE() to the real name inside a larger expression (the two paths
# disagreed). WordPress's multisite and dbDelta logic read the current database
# name this way. The fast-path now reports the connection's selected database, or
# NULL when none is selected, matching MySQL and the parser.
#
# The conformance harness connects both targets to the database `conformance`, so
# the bare forms below return that name. (An expression over DATABASE() goes to
# the parser, which already handled it -- see introspection_fn.test; these bare
# forms exercise the fast-path that was wrong.) Expected to pass against both
# turso-mysql-server and a real mysqld.

# The bare DATABASE() probe.
query
SELECT DATABASE()
----
conformance

# Its synonym SCHEMA(), also bare.
query
SELECT SCHEMA()
----
conformance

# A bare multi-item probe select (still the fast-path) carries the name through,
# including alongside another introspection function and under an alias.
query
SELECT DATABASE(), SCHEMA() AS s
----
conformance	conformance
